{"format":1,"version":0,"generated_at":"2026-09-26T20:33:24.157Z","exam":{"slug":"jamb","name":"JAMB"},"subject":{"slug":"english-language","name":"English Language","display_name":"Use of English"},"topics":[],"papers":[{"id":-1,"year":2025,"title":"Use of English sample questions","duration_minutes":null,"items":[{"id":-1,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>Choose the word that is nearest in meaning to <b>rapid</b>.</p>","options":{"A":"slow","B":"quick","C":"late","D":"weak"},"answer":"B","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>Rapid means fast. Quick is the closest word.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Rapid mean fast. Na quick dey closest.</p>"},{"id":-2,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>She ____ to school every day.</p>","options":{"A":"go","B":"goes","C":"going","D":"gone"},"answer":"B","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>With \"she\" we add -es to the verb in the present tense: she goes.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Wen na \"she\", we add -es to the verb: she goes.</p>"},{"id":-3,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>What is the plural of <i>child</i>?</p>","options":{"A":"childs","B":"childes","C":"children","D":"childrens"},"answer":"C","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>\"Child\" has an irregular plural: children.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>\"Child\" no follow normal rule. The plural na children.</p>"},{"id":-4,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>Choose the word that is opposite in meaning to <b>generous</b>.</p>","options":{"A":"kind","B":"mean","C":"rich","D":"happy"},"answer":"B","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>A generous person gives freely. A mean person does not.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Generous person dey give well well. Mean person no dey give.</p>"},{"id":-5,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>Choose the correct spelling.</p>","options":{"A":"recieve","B":"receive","C":"receve","D":"recive"},"answer":"B","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>Remember: \"i before e, except after c\". So: receive.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Remember: \"i before e, except after c\". So na receive.</p>"},{"id":-6,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>The boys ____ playing football.</p>","options":{"A":"is","B":"am","C":"are","D":"be"},"answer":"C","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>\"Boys\" is plural, so we use \"are\".</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>\"Boys\" plenty, so we use \"are\".</p>"},{"id":-7,"type":"instruction","html":"<p>Read the passage and answer the two questions that follow.<br><br>Ada woke up early, washed her face and went to the market to buy tomatoes. She returned home before noon.</p>"},{"id":-8,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>What did Ada go to the market to buy?</p>","options":{"A":"rice","B":"tomatoes","C":"yams","D":"bread"},"answer":"B","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>The passage says she went to buy tomatoes.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>The passage talk say she go buy tomatoes.</p>"},{"id":-9,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>When did Ada return home?</p>","options":{"A":"at night","B":"before noon","C":"in the evening","D":"after lunch"},"answer":"B","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>The passage says she returned before noon.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>The passage talk say she come back before noon.</p>"},{"id":-10,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>Choose the correct sentence.</p>","options":{"A":"He don't like rice.","B":"He doesn't likes rice.","C":"He doesn't like rice.","D":"He not like rice."},"answer":"C","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>After \"doesn't\" the verb stays in its base form: like.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>After \"doesn't\" the verb no change: like.</p>"},{"id":-11,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>Which word is closest in meaning to <b>honest</b>?</p>","options":{"A":"truthful","B":"lazy","C":"noisy","D":"careless"},"answer":"A","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>An honest person tells the truth.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Honest person dey talk true.</p>"}]}]}